  "reason": "The strongest evidence so far is that scvi_n200 as the RNA encoder dramatically outperforms scgpt (0.725 vs ~0.52), making config_042 (scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, transformer, weighted) the clear best. The next critical question is whether the fusion strategy (weighted vs concat) matters with this superior RNA encoder. With scgpt, weighted narrowly beat concat (0.520 vs 0.507), but the dynamics may differ with scvi_n200's richer representations. Config_013 is a clean single-variable test (only fusion changes from weighted to concat) from the best configuration. Understanding whether concat can match or exceed weighted here will determine which fusion family to exploit in the remaining 5 experiments and whether the weighted fusion's slight edge generalizes across RNA encoders."
}

